From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] feat(wlan): build the MT8163 access point for Linux 6.12

The vendor driver's access point lives in its Wi-Fi Direct part: writing
"A" to /dev/wmtWifi registers ap0, whose wiphy offers NL80211_IFTYPE_AP
with the AP SME in the driver (WIPHY_FLAG_HAVE_AP_SME), so hostapd drives
it over nl80211 and only does the 4-way handshake. The stock build had
CFG_ENABLE_WIFI_DIRECT on for ARM, with the P2P objects in the Makefile;
the import turned it off and dropped them. ADR 0028 needs it for the
setup hotspot.

CONFIG_MTK_MT8163_WIFI_AP builds it, off by default. It also turns on
Wi-Fi Display (CFG_SUPPORT_WFD): the vendor code doesn't build Wi-Fi
Direct without it, and the stock build had both. Enabling Wi-Fi Direct
also compiles P2P branches into shared station code, as in the stock
build, so a station regression can be ruled out by turning the symbol
off.

Ported to the 6.12 cfg80211 API, after the station side:
- change_virtual_intf loses the flags; add_key, get_key, del_key and
  set_default_key, stop_ap and set_bitrate_mask take a link id;
  change_beacon takes cfg80211_ap_update; del_station takes
  station_del_parameters; set_monitor_channel takes the net_device.
- mgmt_frame_register is update_mgmt_frame_registrations, which
  carries the subtype set; the driver still filters probe requests and
  action frames only.
- start_ap takes the channel from its settings (preset_chandef is gone),
  and converts the width to a channel type instead of passing one enum
  for the other.
- cfg80211_scan_done takes cfg80211_scan_info, cfg80211_disconnected
  takes locally_generated, ndo_select_queue takes sb_dev, and the MAC
  address is set with eth_hw_addr_set.
- The station_info for a new client is zeroed: it has grown pointers
  since 3.18, and assoc_req_ies needs no flag any more.
- The testmode prototypes are optional, as on wlan0, instead of an
  #error without CONFIG_NL80211_TESTMODE.
- p2p_fsm.h's ASSERT_BREAK, empty when DBG is 0, no longer replaces
  compat/legacy_time.h's, which the station code was built and tested
  with. Its one use outside a loop becomes ASSERT.

Compiled only (zImage for the Echo family); not run on a device yet.

